name: sim.setVisionSensorCharImage
description:
luaSynopsis: int result=sim.setVisionSensorCharImage(int sensorHandle,buffer image)
pythonSynopsis: int result=sim.setVisionSensorCharImage(int sensorHandle,bytes image)
inputs (possibly taken/adapted from C-function counterpart. Adjust accordingly):
1. sensorHandle: handle of the vision sensor object. Can be combined with sim.handleflag_greyscale (simply add sim.handleflag_greyscale to sensorHandle if you provide grey scale values instead of rgb value) or/and sim.handleflag_rawvalue (simply add sim.handleflag_rawvalue to sensorHandle if you do not wish to trigger image processing).
2. image: rgb buffer containing the image (buffer size must be resolutionX*resolutionY*3). Values in the buffer should vary between 0 and 255. In case a grey scale image is provided, the buffer size must be resolutionX*resolutionY.
outputs (possibly taken/adapted from C-function counterpart. Adjust accordingly):
1. -1 if operation was not successful. 0 if the image processing didn't trigger anything, 1 if the image processing triggered a detection
replacedBy:
- name: image, class: visionSensor, file: visionSensor_image.property
- name: setImage, class: visionSensor, file: visionSensor_setImage.method
